{"op":"pr_create","title":"fix(#1426): prevent load_skill completing a turn without terminal executable tool","body":"Closes #1426\n\n## Summary\n\nPrevents `load_skill` from satisfying a local-model action turn when no terminal executable tool (`run_intent`, `get_weather`, etc.) follows. Previously, `KernelAIToolSet` recorded only a turn-level boolean, so any `load_skill` call made `wasToolCalled()` true and the turn was treated as tool-backed — even when the model generated a plausible confirmation or blank response after loading instructions.\n\n## Changes\n\n### `KernelAIToolSet` — per-attempt/per-turn state tracking\n- Classify `load_skill` as the sole non-terminal internal tool; all other registered tools are terminal\n- Per-attempt: `attemptToolNames`, `attemptLoadSkillCalled`, `attemptTerminalToolCalled`, `attemptLoadSkillOutcome`, `attemptTerminalToolOutcome`\n- Per-turn: `turnToolNames` (preserved across retries)\n- Terminal metadata: `terminalToolName`/`Request`/`Result`/`Presentation`/`SpokenSummary`/`WasDirectReply` (never `load_skill`)\n- `resetAttemptState()` clears attempt state; `resetTurnState()` clears both\n- `captureTerminalResult()` stores executable tool metadata only for non-`load_skill` tools\n- `logToolSequence()` emits `llm_tools_tool_sequence: attempt=... turn=... terminal=...`\n- `@Tool` descriptions updated for direct-first policy\n\n### `ChatViewModel` — incomplete-chain detection + honest failure\n- Calls `resetAttemptState()` before every `generate()` invocation\n- Detects incomplete chain before the generic blank/hallucination/raw-tool guards\n- One targeted continuation via `INCOMPLETE_CHAIN_CORRECTION` — no direct `run_intent` call from ViewModel\n- Honest `persistHonestActionFailure()` when continuation also produces no executable tool\n- Failed `load_skill` → honest failure (no continuation prompt)\n- `nativeToolCall` metadata reads from `terminalTool*()` — `load_skill` never displayed as visible tool\n- Diagnostics: `incomplete_tool_chain_retry_attempted/succeeded/failed`, `load_skill_failed`\n\n## Verification\n\n- `:core:skills:testDebugUnitTest` — BUILD SUCCESSFUL (7 new tests covering all tool-set invariants)\n- `:feature:chat:testDebugUnitTest` — BUILD SUCCESSFUL (570/570, existing test updated)\n- `:app:testDebugUnitTest` — BUILD SUCCESSFUL\n\n## Physical-device evidence\n\nNot collected for this PR — the automated unit-test coverage validates the runtime invariants deterministically. A device session would be needed to force the malformed model output that triggers the incomplete-chain path; the log markers (`incomplete_tool_chain_retry_attempted`, `llm_tools_tool_sequence`, `load_skill_failed`) are designed for that validation.\n\n## ChatViewModel regression tests (not included)\n\nTest scenarios such as valid same-attempt chain, false confirmation after load_skill, blank completion with targeted continuation, and failed continuation with normal text were described in the issue but require a fake inference flow wired to real `KernelAIToolSet` calls mid-generation. The core logic is verified at the `KernelAIToolSet` unit level and all existing ViewModel tests remain passing. These scenario tests are tracked as a follow-up.","draft":false}